{"title":"Functional equation for the zeta function","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>functional equation for Riemann zeta function</b> is a result due to analytic continuation of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_zeta_function\" title=\"Riemann zeta function\">Riemann zeta function</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/78380ea7c8198c2fc2ec42ee52af5523d1e286e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\zeta(s)=2^s\\pi^{s-1}\\sin\\left(\\pi s\\over2\\right)\\Gamma(1-s)\\zeta(1-s)\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Preparation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Preparation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#A_formula_for_in\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">A formula for  in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5211aa0e4af21cc5f79fc5b2c07015ef665a2445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;\\sigma&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /></span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Expansion_of_into_Fourier_series\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Expansion of  into Fourier series</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Evaluation_of\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Evaluation of</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Proof_of_the_functional_equation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof of the functional equation</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functional_equation_for_the_zeta_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Preparation\">Preparation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functional_equation_for_the_zeta_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Preparation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are multiple proofs for the functional equation for Riemann zeta function, and this page presents a light-weighted approach which merely relies on the Fourier series for the first periodic <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bernoulli_polynomial&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Bernoulli polynomial (page does not exist)\">Bernoulli polynomial</a> that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a83075739a5adb1f2e8b34b99c53c6f4fe8c7ce5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B_1(x)\\triangleq\\{x\\}-\\frac12=-\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty{\\sin(2\\pi nx)\\over\\pi n}\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>and the Laplace transform identity that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/51976277e8f1818d2782de272060f9caa10f5dd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{\\Gamma(z)\\over r^z}=\\int_0^\\infty\\tau^{z-1}e^{-z\\tau}\\mathrm d\\tau\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45bf54c5a0c28b9b9dbbac39fc95360d685e63e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\pi/2\\le\\arg z\\le\\pi/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"A_formula_for_in\">A formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031cb95fe26028bb28c91f9ba046b40eca3bc5f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5211aa0e4af21cc5f79fc5b2c07015ef665a2445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;\\sigma&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functional_equation_for_the_zeta_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: A formula for  in\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In this article, we will use the common convention that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/03829c046fff69c7790bc6bb03fc0481c61bcb83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=\\sigma+it$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/198ac82ed1feee7391fd55f14463f1db8e92c931.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma,t\\in\\mathbb R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />. As a result, we say that the original <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dirichlet_series&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Dirichlet series (page does not exist)\">Dirichlet series</a> definition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/2506ef6861d2041a07b3cc58b11f23b92122bd90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta(s)\\triangleq\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty{1\\over k^s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"104\" height=\"48\" /> converges only for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/f/b0f920a6b1ef4bed4c6e1bcbd7a10ff207bf4085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. However, if we were to apply Euler-Maclaurin summation on this definition, we obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/f/bdf72656f52fee99d364b45f27aeda2e657bad11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\zeta(s)=\\frac12+{s\\over s-1}-s\\int_1^\\infty{B_1(x)\\over x^{s+1}}\\mathrm dx\\]\" width=\"273\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>in which we can extend the ROC of the latter integral to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac02eef88cb7357e01994953495b806f68838b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma&gt;-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> via <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integration_by_parts\" title=\"Integration by parts\">integration by parts</a>:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f7a32770497b80626bc35dbae5ba672de833af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\int_1^\\infty{B_1(x)\\over x^{s+1}}\\mathrm dx &amp;=\\left.{B_2(x)\\over2x^{s+1}}\\right|_1^\\infty+{s+1\\over2}\\int_1^\\infty{B_2(x)\\over x^{s+2}}\\mathrm dx \\\\ &amp;={B_2\\over2}+{s+1\\over2}\\int_1^\\infty{B_2(x)\\over x^{s+2}}\\mathrm dx \\end{align*}\" width=\"374\" height=\"93\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5211aa0e4af21cc5f79fc5b2c07015ef665a2445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;\\sigma&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> there is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58abce8de4d2336bef45f2cb45f1a0ab010277fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-s\\int_0^1{B_1(x)\\over x^{s+1}}\\mathrm dx=\\frac12+{1\\over s-1}\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>As a result, we obtain a formula for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031cb95fe26028bb28c91f9ba046b40eca3bc5f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5211aa0e4af21cc5f79fc5b2c07015ef665a2445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1&lt;\\sigma&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/f/17f7dad3735ef01fb50e95e6f0accca2f5545d69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\zeta(s)=-s\\int_0^\\infty{B_1(x)\\over x^{s+1}}\\mathrm dx\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Expansion_of_into_Fourier_series\">Expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d48e2e938d8ea7e0975ebb3de065fe7fbe15691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" /> into <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fourier_series&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Fourier series (page does not exist)\">Fourier series</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functional_equation_for_the_zeta_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Expansion of  into Fourier series\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In order to go deeper, let's plug\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a83075739a5adb1f2e8b34b99c53c6f4fe8c7ce5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[B_1(x)\\triangleq\\{x\\}-\\frac12=-\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty{\\sin(2\\pi nx)\\over\\pi n}\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>into the previously obtained formula, so that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/4/9f4d7b14ae50496d6524a2d0116da6c605546d86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\zeta(s) &amp;=s\\underbrace{\\int_0^\\infty\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty{\\sin(2\\pi nx)\\over n\\pi}{\\mathrm dx\\over x^{s+1}}}_{y=2\\pi nx} \\\\ &amp;=s\\int_0^\\infty\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty{\\sin y\\over n\\pi}{\\mathrm dy/2\\pi n\\over(y/2\\pi n)^{s+1}} \\\\ &amp;=\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty{2s\\over(2\\pi n)^{1-s}}\\int_0^\\infty{\\sin y\\over y^{s+1}}\\mathrm dy \\\\ &amp;=2^s\\pi^{s-1}\\zeta(1-s)\\int_0^\\infty{\\sin y\\over y^{s+1}}\\mathrm dy \\end{align*}\" width=\"266\" height=\"239\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the remaining step is to handle the integral\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Evaluation_of\">Evaluation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe6c8dd11c978fe67bf6ed0027bfe6865776180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\int_0^\\infty{\\sin y\\over y^{s+1}}\\mathrm dy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"93\" height=\"41\" /></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functional_equation_for_the_zeta_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Evaluation of\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler%27s_formula\" title=\"Euler&#39;s formula\">Euler's formula</a>, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a31c272eace8ffd7a050cc22295e9fe41d0388.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin\\theta={e^{i\\theta}-e^{-i\\theta}\\over2i}\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>As a result, we only need to calculate\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/0932d5be7cf449d4261bda94d57d4784ac593fd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_0^\\infty{e^{\\pm iy}\\over y^{s+1}}\\mathrm dy\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>if we want to take down the remaining integral. According to Laplace transform identities, we can see that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093edd1fb962cb9d9167414c658063c2580ce952.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_0^\\infty{e^{\\pm iy}\\over y^{s+1}}\\mathrm dy=\\int_0^\\infty y^{-s-1}e^{-e^{\\mp i\\pi/2}y}\\mathrm dy=\\Gamma(-s)e^{\\mp i\\pi s/2}\\]\" width=\"404\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Thus we deduce\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc1a48891a5c6d3f063f6309cb780f4d523590d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\int_0^\\infty{\\sin y\\over y^{s+1}}\\mathrm dy=-\\Gamma(-s)\\sin\\left(\\pi s\\over2\\right)\\]\" width=\"249\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>wherein the RHS serves to be a meromorphic continuation of the LHS integral.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_of_the_functional_equation\">Proof of the functional equation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functional_equation_for_the_zeta_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Proof of the functional equation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>With everything ready, we can put everything together and obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf566a1ccbc4bc8847ff3a2fe50aa6a1fb2a2136.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\zeta(s)=2^s\\pi^{s-1}\\sin\\left(\\pi s\\over2\\right)(-s)\\Gamma(-s)\\zeta(1-s)\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>and by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce50084c690026fcc6bbbb363b91247d50dcf2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma(z+1)=z\\Gamma(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />, this identity becomes the functional equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/78380ea7c8198c2fc2ec42ee52af5523d1e286e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\zeta(s)=2^s\\pi^{s-1}\\sin\\left(\\pi s\\over2\\right)\\Gamma(1-s)\\zeta(1-s)\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Functional_equation_for_the_zeta_function&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Titchmarsh, E. C., <i>The Theory of the Riemann Zeta-Function.</i> Oxford Univ. Press, London and New York, 1951.</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018085059\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 163/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7251/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20340:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018085059 and revision id 142009. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}